# Thirty Factor — mobile feasibility

When proposing, reviewing, or building anything in Thirty Factor Authentication, **always** account for mobile (touch, ~≤500px via `mobileWidthBreakpoint`), not only desktop.

## Feedback & design

- Call out mobile risk early: hit targets, finger-as-cursor, overlays, drag/DnD, tiny text, viewport chrome, safe areas.
- Prefer one-screen or short flows on phone; multi-room / precision-aim / hover-only ideas need a mobile plan or an explicit desktop-primary tradeoff.
- If a level is likely painful on touch, say so before expanding scope.

## Implementation defaults

- Use `isMobile` from level `ContentProps` (or `useIsMobile(mobileWidthBreakpoint)`) for layout, hit slop, and copy ("tap" vs "click").
- Touch targets ≥ ~44px where players must aim; enlarge props or add invisible hit padding on mobile.
- Full-viewport overlays (`position: fixed` / portals): no `transform` on `#auth-container`; leave room for bottom UI / home indicator (`env(safe-area-inset-*)`).
- Finger-as-flashlight / aim: sync light to the tap point; soften lit/aim checks on mobile; don't require mouse-style sweeping.
- Inventory / message chrome should not cover critical props; park interactables away from the auth card and bottom UI band on small screens.
- Drag: prefer pointer events or existing touch DnD patterns; avoid hover-only affordances.

## When unsure

Ship a thinner mobile path (bigger targets, fewer props, clearer tap flow) rather than assuming desktop controls will transfer.
